+++ b/diagnostic/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Experimental f2 numerical and terminal-pricing diagnostic
+
+We derive this source from exact `f2c9e205bd1ecc9afb45d5efe7fcb0df881f2b33`. We preserve that control and its correction=false setting. The derivative checks the 2 descending Compose searches before indexing, records an invalid operation and exits with code 86. It supplies no replacement composition. Valid guard and call-snapshot operations allocate no memory in the local synthetic gate.
+
+We retain only scalar call-entry policy and a bounded raw-dual snapshot during pricing. We serialize the terminal task after `BCP::Run` returns. Eligibility requires the C104_100 root-only completed case, an Exact/Finished/empty final call, no forbidden arcs, unchanged row/cut counts and matching callback generations. We preserve all ordered master cuts and raw duals separately from the original EPS-filtered native query. We reload the pinned native input after BCP returns and verify its SHA-256 before parsing, without adding a pre-solve deep copy. The artifact records actual stored forward/reverse functions, cached intervals, graph order and LDT tables using exact double bits. We never reconstruct these functions through `AddPiece` for serialization.
+
+The [schema](SCHEMA.json) defines every field. Artifacts use exclusive creation and an envelope whose complete marker is written last. Invalid indexing exits with 86. Capture failure exits with 87. An ordinary deadline retains its original native status and produces an explicit no-terminal-capture reason. Every closure event is marked as an uncredited diagnostic phase, and final native output carries diagnostic-only metadata. These artifacts establish no accepted closure.
+
+We run deterministic local gates with the following command from a suitable development environment.
+
+```bash
+python diagnostic/run_local_gates.py --reference-goc /path/to/exact-f2/code/goc --cplex-include /path/to/cplex/include --output /new/local/gate-directory
+```
+
+The gate compiles only the numerical/capture-state fixture and its required translation units. It never runs BCP or a routing solver. It tests invalid and valid composition, original-f2 bitwise valid outputs, deferred call-sequence state, sub-EPS cut dual retention, zero depot coefficients, invalid vertex rejection, raw-buffer bounds, filtered-context consistency, exclusive publication and partial-record rejection. Compiler output and every test outcome remain in the new output directory.
+
+The reproducible package includes source and patch inventories, an unchanged original-f2 numerical reference subset, and a reserved-compute build driver. The build driver builds `bp` and runs synthetic gates only. It does not reserve resources or launch a routing instance. Source-level intended equivalence does not guarantee equal search trajectories because instrumentation can affect layout and timing. Routing reachability, terminal capture on C104, native work equality, same-source replay and cross-engine replay remain untested or unimplemented in this delivery.
